/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:125:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:126:Assemble scattered jigsaw sprites around a central yellow anchor by pairing red connector pixels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:127:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:128:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:129:- bg = black (0). Several colored sprites scattered on the grid.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:130:- One anchor sprite contains a 3×3 yellow (4) block.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:131:- Each sprite has red (2) connector pixels along its edges.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:132:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:133:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:134:- The anchor stays in place; remaining sprites attach one at a time.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:135:- Each sprite is translated so that one of its red pixels overlaps an unpaired red pixel on the growing assembly.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:136:- Every red connector must pair with exactly one other, forming a complete joined structure.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:137:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:138:Key insight: Red pixels act as jigsaw pegs — each must match exactly one counterpart, and the assembly order is determined by which unpaired connectors remain.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:139:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:140:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:141:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:142:<reference_puzzle index="8" source="train" puzzle_id="7ec998c9" lines="14-28">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:143:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:144:Draw a blue folded corner-to-corner route through the lone marker's column.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:145:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:146:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:147:- A rectangular grid filled with one background color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:148:- Exactly one non-background marker pixel; blue is absent from the input.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:149:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:150:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:151:- Preserve the marker and repaint background pixels in its column blue from top to bottom.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:152:- If the marker is in the unique center column, connect that column to the top-right and bottom-left corners.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:153:- Otherwise, connect the column to the top-left and bottom-right corners.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:154:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:155:Key insight:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:156:The marker's column is the route spine; its central vs off-center placement selects which opposite corner pair gets the horizontal edge segments.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:157:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:158:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:159:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:160:<reference_puzzle index="9" source="eval" puzzle_id="7c66cb00" lines="9-24">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:161:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:162:Dock two-tone sprites into color-matched horizontal bars with a color swap.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:163:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:164:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:165:- bg = most common color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:166:- Top area: small two-tone sprites (outer color + inner color).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:167:- Below: horizontal bars spanning most of the row, each with a fill color and border color on edges.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:168:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:169:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:170:- Match each sprite to the bar whose fill color equals the sprite's outer color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:171:- Place the sprite at its original x-position, aligned to the bar's bottom.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:172:- Recolor: sprite outer → bar border, sprite inner → bar fill.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:173:- Erase original sprites from the top area.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:174:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:175:Key insight: Color matching is inverted — the sprite's dominant color identifies its target bar, then gets swapped to the bar's accent color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:176:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:177:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:178:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:179:<reference_puzzle index="10" source="eval" puzzle_id="2b83f449" lines="10-22">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:180:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:181:Simulate tokens falling through a pipe network after gates rotate open.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:182:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:183:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:184:- Wall (0), bg (pipe fill), gate (horizontal 1×3 bars), token (small edge pixels).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:185:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:186:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:187:- Rotate each gate into a vertical blocker; gate cells become bg.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:188:- Tokens drop downward through bg, choosing the extreme column for their side (left→min, right→max).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:189:- Tokens settle at true pipe ends (adjacent to wall/boundary), packing inward.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:190:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:191:Key insight: Tokens select drop columns by entry side and land at wall-bounded endpoints, ignoring blocker-bounded ones.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:192:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:193:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:194:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:195:<reference_puzzle index="11" source="train" puzzle_id="4a1cacc2" lines="8-23">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:196:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:197:Fill the rectangle from the lone foreground pixel to its nearest grid corner.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:198:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:199:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:200:- The grid is a uniform background field with exactly one foreground pixel.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:201:- The foreground pixel's color is the color used for all added pixels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:202:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:203:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:204:- Find the grid corner with the smallest Manhattan distance to the foreground pixel.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:205:- Recolor every pixel in the inclusive axis-aligned rectangle bounded by that
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:206:  corner and the foreground pixel to the foreground color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:207:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:208:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:209:- The single pixel is one corner of the rectangle; the opposite corner is the
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:210:  nearest corner of the whole canvas.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:211:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:212:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:213:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:214:<reference_puzzle index="12" source="train" puzzle_id="41ace6b5" lines="7-26">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:215:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:216:Normalize vertical two-color bars between paired marker columns around the marker rows.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:217:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:218:Input structure
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:219:- The background is the dominant color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:220:- A row of red marker pixels sits directly above a row of gray marker pixels
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:221:  in the same alternating columns.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:222:- The columns between adjacent markers contain vertical bars made from a
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:223:  contiguous teal run above a contiguous blue run.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:224:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:225:Rule
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:226:- Keep the marker pixels and all non-bar background cells fixed.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:227:- Let h be the maximum teal-run height among the bar columns; paint teal in
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:228:  every bar column for h rows ending at the red marker row.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:229:- In each bar column, move its blue run to start at the gray marker row and
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:230:  fill all lower cells in that column with maroon.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:231:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:232:Key insight
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:233:- The marker rows are a baseline: teal is normalized into a common upper
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:234:  band, while each blue run keeps its own height below the baseline.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:235:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:236:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:237:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:238:<reference_puzzle index="13" source="eval" puzzle_id="b99e7126" lines="34-48">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:239:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:240:Scale a minority cell's inner pattern up to the cell-grid level, completing a fractal overlay.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:241:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:242:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:243:- Grid divided into NxN cells by separator lines of a single color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:244:- Most cells share an identical interior pattern (majority); a few have a distinct pattern (minority).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:245:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:246:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:247:- Extract the inner pixel pattern from the minority cell.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:248:- Treat each pixel as a cell-sized stamp: active pixels → minority pattern, inactive → majority pattern.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:249:- Position this scaled-up pattern on the cell grid so existing minority cells align with active pixels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:250:- Fill in all remaining active positions with the minority pattern.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:251:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:252:Key insight: The minority cell's interior is a miniature blueprint of where minority cells should appear at the grid scale — fractal self-similarity.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:253:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:254:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:255:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:256:<reference_puzzle index="14" source="train" puzzle_id="1b59e163" lines="54-69">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:257:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:258:Copy each marked sprite to every standalone marker of the same color and erase the original sources.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:259:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:260:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:261:- The background is the dominant color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:262:- Each source is an 8-connected component containing a monochrome sprite and one marker pixel of another color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:263:- Other isolated marker pixels may be destinations; marker colors with no source sprite are distractors.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:264:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:265:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:266:- Clear the grid to background.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:267:- For every source marker color, place the sprite at each other marker of that color using the source marker as the anchor.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:268:- Keep each destination marker pixel in place; do not keep source sprites, source markers, or distractor markers.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:269:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:270:Key insight:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:271:- A colored marker is not part of the sprite geometry; it is the anchor that says where same-colored copies of that sprite should be stamped.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:272:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:273:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:274:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:275:<reference_puzzle index="15" source="eval" puzzle_id="3e6067c3" lines="7-20">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:276:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:277:Connect framed squares via colored bridges following a control-pixel sequence.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:278:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:279:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:280:- bg = background. Border color forms equal-sized framed squares with unique inner fill colors.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:281:- Control row below squares: colored pixels read left-to-right encode visitation order.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:282:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:283:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:284:- Start at the square matching first control color c0.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:285:- For each consecutive pair (ci, ci+1), find the ci+1-colored square aligned in the same row or column band, preferring nearest.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:286:- Draw a bridge colored ci between the pair, spanning the gap with inner-square thickness.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:287:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:288:Key insight: Row/column-band alignment plus proximity resolves ambiguity when inner colors repeat.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:289:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:290:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:291:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:292:<reference_puzzle index="16" source="eval" puzzle_id="898e7135" lines="7-20">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:293:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:294:Inflate a frame's hole-layout and fill each hole with its matching piece.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:295:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:296:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:297:- bg = most common color. Largest component is a monochrome frame enclosing bg holes.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:298:- Outside pieces composed of k×k blocks; k = side of smallest solid square piece.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:299:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:300:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:301:- Extract connected hole regions inside the frame as slots.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:302:- Match each piece to a slot by comparing block-level shapes under rotation/flip.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:303:- Output the layout scaled by k, with pieces placed in slots; frame color as background.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:304:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:305:Key insight: Pieces are k×k-block-scaled versions of holes; downsampling reveals shape matches under all 8 orientations.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed241687935/5/prompt.md:306:</description>
